\fs6\
\pard \s39 \li2520 \fi-604 \ri1007 \ql \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1  (void)\b setBorderType:\b0 (NSBorderType)\i aType\i0  \
\fs14\
\fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Sets the border type to \i aType\i0 , which must be a valid border type. Border types are defined in \b NSView.h\b0 ; currently, the following border types are defined:\
\fs14\
\pard \s4 \li2338 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx2338 \tx3753 \tx4146 \fs28 NSNoBorder\
\fi0 NSLineBorder\
\fi0 NSBezelBorder\
\fi0 NSGrooveBorder\
\fs14\
\pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 \fs28 If the size of the new border is different from that of the old border, the content view is resized to absorb the difference and the box is marked for redisplay.\
\fs14\
\pard \s57 \li2804 \fi-1292 \ri1007 \ql \tx2799 \tx3282 \tx3771 \fs28 \f0 \b \fs24 See also:\tab \f1 \b0 \fs28 \b \f3 -\f1 \'80setNeedsDisplay:\b0  (NSView)\
\fs14\
