\fs6\
\pard \s39 \li2520 \fi-604 \ri1007 \ql \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1  (void)\b setTitleFont:\b0 (NSFont *)\i aFont\
\fs14\
\i0 \fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Sets \i aFont\i0  as the NSFont object used to draw the NSBox\'27s title, and marks the region of the receiver within the title rectangle as needing display. On Mach systems the title is drawn using the 12.0 point system font by default. If the size of the new font is different from that of the old font, the content view is resized to absorb the difference.\
\fs14\
\pard \s57 \li2804 \fi-1292 \ri1007 \ql \tx2799 \tx3282 \tx3771 \fs28 \f0 \b \fs24 See also:\tab \f1 \b0 \fs28 \b \f3 -\f1 \'80setNeedsDisplayInRect:\b0  (NSView)\
