¬}\pard \s40 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx8265 setTitlePosition:\
\fs6\
\pard \s39 \li2520 \fi-604 \ri1007 \ql \f1 \b0 \fs28 \f3 -\f1  (void)\b setTitlePosition:\b0 (NSTitlePosition)\i aPosition\i0  \
\fs14\
\fs28 \pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 Sets the title position to \i aPosition\i0 , which can be one of the values listed in the following table. The default position is NSAtTop.\
\fs14\
\pard \s62 \li1915 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx6753 \tx9553 \f0 \b \fs28 Value\tab Meaning\
\fs6\
\pard \s60 \li6753 \fi-4838 \ri1007 \ql \tx6753 \tx9525 \f1 \b0 \fs28 NSNoTitle\tab The box has no title\
\fs14\
\fs28 NSAboveTop\tab Title positioned above the box\'27s top border\
\fs14\
\fs28 NSAtTop\tab Title positioned within the box\'27s top border\
\fs14\
\fs28 NSBelowTop\tab Title positioned below the box\'27s top border\
\fs14\
\fs28 NSAboveBottom\tab Title positioned above the box\'27s bottom border\
\fs14\
\fs28 NSAtBottom\tab Title positioned within the box\'27s bottom border\
\fs14\
\fs28 NSBelowBottom\tab Title positioned below the box\'27s bottom border\
\fs14\
\pard \s3 \li1512 \fi0 \ri1007 \ql \tx3603 \tx3981 \tx4359 \fs28 If the new title position changes the size of the box\'27s border area, the content view is resized to absorb the difference, and the box is marked as needing redisplay.\
\fs14\
